{"id":"agents-root","ord":"a0","title":"Agents","desc":"Who can be dispatched — one node per agent, `command`/`role` as props. The `command` value is THE EXACT LAUNCH COMMAND, run verbatim; a missing row, or a row without `command`, REFUSES the spawn loudly — nobody falls back to a machine default. Spawn shape: `kolu create --repo <repo> --worktree <branch> -- <command>` (or the MCP equivalent). The rule nodes governing reviewing and choosing sit at this outline's TOP LEVEL, after this roster (the human's placement, 2026-08-29).","changed":"2026-08-29T13:12:28-04:00"}
{"id":"agent-claude-opus","parent":"agents-root","ord":"a0","title":"claude-opus — the author agent","desc":"Claude Code pinned to Opus with the 1M context window, YOLO mode. The default author for dispatched lanes. Verify with the banner at spawn: it must say Opus, not the machine default.\n\nTUI quirk: the composer's `❯` line shows PLACEHOLDER text (a suggestion or echo that was never typed) — it is NOT an unsent draft; never treat a populated-looking composer as pending human input. Applies to all Claude Code TUIs, fable included.","changed":"2026-08-26T20:09:56-04:00","custom":{"command":"claude --model opus[1m] --dangerously-skip-permissions","concurrency":"HARD CAP: at most THREE concurrent Claude Opus AUTHOR lanes (daily-limit reasons); Opus REVIEWERS are exempt and do not count; grok/pi are outside the cap. The orchestrator queues further Opus work until a slot frees.","context":"1M — the [1m] suffix pins it everywhere (native on the API; a lane that runs for hours must not compact itself into amnesia)","role":"author"}}
{"id":"agent-grok","parent":"agents-root","ord":"a1","title":"grok — author and reviewer","desc":"Grok CLI in always-approve mode. Reviews in a split of the author's worktree; proven author on infra-shaped and test-shaped work (its one UI authoring attempt was discarded — prefer Opus for UI/design-heavy).\n\nTUI quirk: a message sent while grok is mid-turn is QUEUED by default — after text → settle → Enter, if the screen shows the message queued rather than steering, press Enter once more.","changed":"2026-08-26T20:10:00-04:00","custom":{"command":"grok --always-approve","role":"author+reviewer","usage-limit":"Do NOT re-dispatch grok lanes on a low weekly-limit reading (the human can raise it); if a session actually dies on the limit, tell the human and wait.","watch-item":"Once spawned its OWN reviewer instead of reporting — reviewers are the orchestrator's to dispatch; authors report and stop. Watch for recurrence."}}
{"id":"agent-claude-fable","parent":"agents-root","ord":"a3","title":"claude-fable — design-grade author","desc":"Claude Code pinned to Fable (the Mythos-tier model above Opus), YOLO mode. For design-first work only — the expensive tier; Opus stays the default author. Verify with the banner: it must say Fable.","created":"2026-08-19T20:04:37-04:00","changed":"2026-08-26T20:10:11-04:00","custom":{"command":"claude --model fable --dangerously-skip-permissions","role":"author"}}
{"id":"agent-pi","parent":"agents-root","ord":"a2V","title":"pi — reviewer (kimi-k3)","desc":"The pi CLI on its default model (kimi-k3). **IMPLEMENTOR SEAT REMOVED (the human, 2026-09-01): opencode replaces pi as the kimi implementor — pi is a REVIEWER only now.** Proven at the complex end as a reviewer; its authoring history stands in git and the compaction ledger. Boots to a plain composer fast; the status bar's token counters are the working signal.","created":"2026-08-24T16:40:49-04:00","changed":"2026-09-01T15:23:32-04:00","custom":{"command":"pi","glitch-note":"kimi-k3 serving is the fragile part: known failure shapes are raw special-token emissions mid-tool-call (restart fresh in the same worktree with a resume pointer) and full-pool 429 outages. pi and opencode SHARE the Juspay kimi pool — they are not fallbacks for each other.","model":"kimi-k3 (pi's own default; no flag needed)","review-rule":"pi-authored PRs take BOTH grok AND Claude Opus as reviewers","role":"reviewer","watch-item":"Overruns role boundaries when the next step is obvious (has run suites as reviewer; once merged its own PR). Briefs for pi state the stop-lines explicitly; watch every lane."}}
{"id":"agent-opencode","parent":"agents-root","ord":"a5","title":"opencode — the kimi implementor","desc":"**THE KIMI IMPLEMENTOR (the human, 2026-09-01, replacing pi — the alternation experiment closes):** opencode is the kimi-k3 commodity author. opencode TUI on its configured model (kimi-k3 via Juspay — shares the pool pi used, and its outages). Quirks: has mislabeled itself \"codex\" in a posted review (brief it to title reviews with its tool name); its no-drift claims have been wrong before — weigh them accordingly; a message sent mid-turn QUEUES (no interrupt method).","changed":"2026-09-01T15:23:32-04:00","custom":{"command":"opencode","role":"author"}}
{"id":"roster-reviewer-contract","ord":"a1","title":"The reviewer contract","desc":"A reviewer's job is READING THE CODE — the diff, the code around it, whether the PR body's claims hold, what breaks that nobody tested. Reviewers do NOT run test suites, ever; one surgical probe of ONE specific claim is allowed only where reading cannot settle it — never a suite, never e2e. Delivery: work in a split of the author's worktree, post ONE comment via gh (verdict + MUST/SHOULD/NIT at file:line), never edit/push/merge. Every review brief carries this contract in its header. An author never reviews its own lane. Reviewer pairing follows the tier rule on the choosing node (2026-08-28): mechanical lanes take a commodity reviewer, ordinary lanes take claude-opus, design-heavy Opus-authored lanes take grok/pi; pi-authored lanes take BOTH grok and claude-opus.","created":"2026-08-26T20:09:46-04:00","changed":"2026-08-29T13:12:20-04:00"}
{"id":"roster-choosing","ord":"a2","title":"Choosing an implementor","desc":"**THE TIER RULE (the human, 2026-08-28; the third tier re-founded 2026-08-29):** every lane is tiered at dispatch, the tier written as a `tier` prop (values: mechanical, ordinary, design-heavy). Opus is the default REVIEWER, not the default author.\n\n- **mechanical** — deletions, renames, config edits, doc moves, pin bumps, flake fixes. Commodity author AND commodity reviewer; Opus never enters the lane.\n- **ordinary** — bounded features and bugfixes. Commodity author; **claude-opus reviews**. (Provenance: #417 — Opus review found the MUSTs the commodity reviewer missed.)\n- **design-heavy** — RE-FOUNDED (the human, 2026-08-29, approved): design is always settled before dispatch, so this tier no longer means \"unsettled design\" — it means the FACTORS say the implementation itself wants Opus hands. **claude-opus authors when ANY of:**\n  1. **core seam or wide blast radius** — the diff touches the format grammar, addresses/routing, fold/focus, the wire, or 3+ packages;\n  2. **distant invariants** — the change must uphold promises declared in files it does not edit;\n  3. **no precedent** — the repo holds no existing instance of the pattern to imitate;\n  4. **facts tests cannot pin** — correctness hinges on kernel/OS/wire truths where a wrong premise ships confidently.\n  **Tie-breaker:** a wrong turn that costs a fix round → the kimi author (Opus review catches it cheaply); one that costs a rewrite → Opus. (Provenance: #428's two MUSTs were cross-cutting invariant breaks and #426's was a wrong PDEATHSIG premise — pi-authored lanes with fully settled designs.) claude-fable on the human's word; reviewers per the pairing rules (an author never reviews its own lane).\n\n**THE KIMI SEAT IS OPENCODE'S (the human, 2026-09-01, closing the 2026-08-31 alternation experiment):** opencode is the kimi-k3 commodity author; pi no longer implements and stays on the roster as a reviewer only — the compaction ledger beside this roster holds the record that decided it. Grok's place is unchanged: grok when opencode is occupied, the pool is down, or the work is plainly grok-shaped (infra/test mechanics). Standing rules that survive: a kimi-authored lane takes BOTH grok and claude-opus as reviewers; flake lanes are commodity, never Opus; when the human names an agent, their word wins over everything here.\n\n**THE RULE LEARNS:** the board's `took`/`musts`/`shoulds` props are the dataset — the compaction ledger is now part of it — revisit these factors with numbers when enough lanes carry them.","created":"2026-08-26T20:09:47-04:00","changed":"2026-09-01T15:23:32-04:00"}
{"id":"agent-claude-ci","parent":"agents-root","ord":"a6","title":"claude-ci — the CI watcher (Sonnet)","desc":"**RETIRED (the human's ban, 2026-09-01 night): claude-ci is banned from CI — the orchestrator runs odu itself, and dag-pr-ci carries the law. This row stands as history only; it is never spawned again.**\n\nClaude Code pinned to Sonnet, YOLO mode, with odu's MCP attached at launch (`--mcp-config orchestrator/ci-watcher-mcp.json`). Was the CI-WATCHER SEAT (an interim seat from 2026-08-29): spawned as a split of the author's terminal at close, briefed from orchestrator/ci-watcher.md (deleted with the retirement; git history keeps both), it launched and followed CI and reported flakes + reds. Its last act: #461's watcher, banned and killed mid-flight on 2026-09-01, its run cancelled cleanly and relaunched by the orchestrator's own hands.","created":"2026-08-29T10:20:48-04:00","changed":"2026-09-01T20:18:25-04:00","custom":{"command":"claude --model sonnet --dangerously-skip-permissions --strict-mcp-config --mcp-config /home/srid/code/oss.olai/orchestrator/ci-watcher-mcp.json","role":"ci-watcher"}}
{"id":"kimi-compaction-ledger","ord":"a3","title":"The kimi-k3 compaction ledger — pi vs opencode","desc":"THE EXPERIMENT, CLOSED (opened by the human 2026-08-31; ruled by them 2026-09-01): pi and opencode alternated as the kimi-k3 commodity author with every auto-compaction incident recorded here, and the human ruled for OPENCODE — it replaces pi as the implementor; pi stays a reviewer. The record that decided it: pi — three overflows in one lane on 2026-08-31 (all survived), a fourth on odu-doorbell 2026-09-01 (outcome pending at the ruling), plus two raw-token-spill session restarts the same day; opencode — one overflow on odu-checkout-targeting, survived fully coherent mid-refactor. The ledger stays as history; new incidents still land here while any kimi agent authors.","created":"2026-08-31T12:53:10-04:00","changed":"2026-09-01T15:23:17-04:00"}
{"id":"kcl-pi-fdo-1","parent":"kimi-compaction-ledger","ord":"a0","title":"pi · file-delete-op · overflow #1 · survived","desc":"2026-08-31 ~11:36, ~4 minutes into the lane: 98.3% of 256k (11M tokens read — wide file sweeps), response truncated mid-edit, auto-compacted, resumed coherent at 133k and continued implementing correctly.","created":"2026-08-31T12:53:10-04:00"}
{"id":"kcl-pi-fdo-2","parent":"kimi-compaction-ledger","ord":"a1","title":"pi · file-delete-op · overflow #2 · survived","desc":"2026-08-31 ~12:47, mid-evidence (playwright shots against a local server): 98.4% of 256k again (58M tokens read cumulative), response truncated, auto-compacted. Resumed coherent at 19% and continued the same debugging thread (found its own template-literal escaping bug on the first post-compaction turn — continuity held). Implementation still uncommitted on disk at this point; noted that pi is hand-rolling screenshot tooling in /tmp rather than the saatchi recipe.","created":"2026-08-31T12:53:10-04:00","changed":"2026-08-31T13:02:58-04:00"}
{"id":"kcl-pi-fdo-3","parent":"kimi-compaction-ledger","ord":"a2","title":"pi · file-delete-op · overflow #3 · survived (at report boundary)","desc":"2026-08-31 ~14:14, the instant its address-round report finished (96.3% of 256k, 94M tokens read cumulative): auto-compacted with the work already pushed at 77e65bc1 — the safest possible timing; nothing owed from the dying window. Three overflows in one lane, all survived coherent.","created":"2026-08-31T14:15:03-04:00"}
{"id":"kcl-opencode-oct-1","parent":"kimi-compaction-ledger","ord":"a3","title":"opencode · odu checkout-targeting · overflow #1 · survived","desc":"2026-09-01 ~14:25 ET, during the refactor passes: observed at 215.4K/84% mid-step, then 60.1K/23% with the step complete — an auto-compaction between two orchestrator reads (the moment itself unobserved). Survived fully coherent: both refactor passes landed as isolated commits with a proper report, non-findings documented, 524/0 unit runs serially after each pass, zero test files touched.","created":"2026-09-01T14:33:01-04:00"}
{"id":"kcl-pi-odb-1","parent":"kimi-compaction-ledger","ord":"a4","title":"pi · odu-doorbell · overflow #1 · outcome pending","desc":"2026-09-01 ~15:00 ET, session 2 of the lane (session 1 was restarted for token spills, not compaction): mid-evidence preparation (writing the saatchi section + a mod.just PATH knob), response truncated at 97.8% of 256k (29M read), auto-compaction started. Outcome to be recorded when the session resumes: coherent / thrashed / restarted.","created":"2026-09-01T15:00:40-04:00"}
{"id":"kcl-pi-obi-1","parent":"kimi-compaction-ledger","ord":"a5","title":"pi · odu-baked-in · overflow #1 · outcome pending","desc":"2026-09-02 ~01:47 UTC, mid-address on #464 (the two e2e MUSTs): response truncated at 98.6% of 256k (31M read), auto-compaction started. Outcome to be recorded when the session resumes.","created":"2026-09-01T21:47:23-04:00"}
